From: UAF Injection Patch 008
Subject: [PATCH] UAF in jquant2.c: stale histogram[0] after premature free

Vulnerability type : Use-After-Free
File               : jquant2.c
Function           : jinit_2pass_quantizer
Trigger            : cinfo->desired_number_of_colors == 256
Difficulty         : Low — 256 is the default desired_number_of_colors

The injection adds a conditional free() of cquantize->histogram[0] inside
jinit_2pass_quantizer() when the desired number of colors is 256 (the default).
The prescan_quantize and select_colors functions later read through the freed
histogram slice, causing a heap use-after-free.
Pattern P5 (realloc-invalidation).

diff --git a/jquant2.c b/jquant2.c
index 44efb18..3362b28 100644
--- a/jquant2.c
+++ b/jquant2.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #define JPEG_INTERNALS
 #include "jinclude.h"
 #include "jpeglib.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 #ifdef QUANT_2PASS_SUPPORTED
 
@@ -1243,6 +1244,23 @@ jinit_2pass_quantizer(j_decompress_ptr cinfo)
   }
   cquantize->needs_zeroed = TRUE; /* histogram is garbage now */
 
+  /*
+   * BUG INJECTION (UAF-008):
+   * When the desired number of colors is exactly 256, free histogram[0]
+   * simulating a failed realloc-style resize.  The prescan_quantize and
+   * select_colors functions still read through the freed histogram slice.
+   */
+#ifndef MAGMA_ENABLE_FIXES
+#ifdef MAGMA_ENABLE_CANARIES
+  MAGMA_LOG("JPGUAF08", cinfo->desired_number_of_colors == 256);
+#endif
+  if (cinfo->desired_number_of_colors == 256) {
+    free(cquantize->histogram[0]);
+    MAGMA_FREE_LOG("JPGUAF08");
+    /* pointer is NOT nulled — dangling reference remains in histogram[0] */
+  }
+#endif
+
   /* Allocate storage for the completed colormap, if required.
    * We do this now since it may affect the memory manager's space
    * calculations.
